speechtext:
The system adopted by the Distribution office is an excellent one. I refer to the system of sending out to institutions cards containing a list of public documents that are available and leaving to the parties the selection of documents which they want. By this work I think a great saving can be accomplished.
Expenses under the Canada Temperance Act.
$1,000. [DOT] ( {

My hon. friend has
brought this matter before one a number of times during the last three months. I have made inquiries, and I find a report from the engineer that it would require 6ome $15,000 or $30,000 to do this work. I have information from a gentleman in whom I have the very greatest confidence that about $2,000 will do it. I am going to investigate the matter. There is a general vote for the Maritime Provinces, and if the work can be done for a reasonable sum of money, I may be able to arrange to do it out of the general fund. I shall, however, have the matter thoroughly investigated and do whatever is proper.
Dredging-Ontario and Quebec, further amount required, $70,000;
